      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This translation of “Adonai boker e’erokh lekha” by Rabbi David Aaron de Sola of a piyyut by an unknown paytan was first published in his <tei:hi rend="italic">Ancient Melodies of the Spanish and Portuguese Jews</tei:hi> (1857). The Hebrew text of this piyyut was found in a Siddur published in Venice in 1598, found at Hebrewbooks.org by Abe Katz (Burei haTefila Institute) where it appears on the recto and verso of page 8. (Thank you!) –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
